\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The arrangement of nanoparticles in Fig.1 in \cite  {Saccone2022}. (a) Original picture, (b) Image processing for particle position and orientation of their easy axes. Recovered shape of particles is shown by black elliptical outline for each particle. The long axis of an ellipse indicates the easy axis of the particle. Every particle is numbered by its center position from bottom to top for further filtering and consisting sub-lattices. Some truncated particles are filtered with an appropriate condition.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.6}}
\newlabel{fig:sac1}{{1}{5}{The arrangement of nanoparticles in Fig.1 in \cite {Saccone2022}. (a) Original picture, (b) Image processing for particle position and orientation of their easy axes. Recovered shape of particles is shown by black elliptical outline for each particle. The long axis of an ellipse indicates the easy axis of the particle. Every particle is numbered by its center position from bottom to top for further filtering and consisting sub-lattices. Some truncated particles are filtered with an appropriate condition.\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Temperature vs heat capacity in sub-lattices of various sizes calculated by the enumeration and Monte-Carlo method. Peaks in lower temperature appear in only Monte-Carlo method so could be ignored. A small shift is found between curves.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.8}}
\newlabel{fig:capSac}{{2}{5}{Temperature vs heat capacity in sub-lattices of various sizes calculated by the enumeration and Monte-Carlo method. Peaks in lower temperature appear in only Monte-Carlo method so could be ignored. A small shift is found between curves.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
